title: Webfont Tiddler

A font is stored as a single stylesheet tiddler: the font file is embedded in the `@font-face` rule as a base64 data URI, so nothing is fetched from the network and the font works offline and in single-file wikis.

|!Title|`$:/fonts/<font name>`|
|!Tags|`$:/tags/Stylesheet`|
|!Type|`text/css`|
|!Index fields|`font-family`, `font-format`, `font-type` (sans, serif, mono, script, fantasy), `note`|

```css
@font-face {
    font-family: "<font name>";
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    src: url(data:font/woff2;base64,<<<CODE>>>) format("woff2");
}
```

!! Creating one

Drop a `.woff2`, `.woff`, `.ttf` or `.otf` file onto the wiki and confirm the import: the plugin builds the tiddler above for you. `.ttf` and `.otf` files are converted to WOFF2 on the way in (see the plugin's settings).

To write one by hand, create a tiddler with the title, tag and type above and paste the `@font-face` rule, with `src` last.

